   "evidence": "Line 208 `:= (rfl)`; the definition `FDRep.frobeniusSchurIndicator V := Representation.frobeniusSchurIndicator V.\u03c1` (line 205) makes the theorem hold by unfolding one definition, unaffected by the parentheses.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/CharacterTable/FrobeniusSchur.lean",
   "fix": "Drop the parentheses (use `rfl`) and remove the sentence about parentheses controlling defeq export; the preceding sentence about not `@[expose]`-ing the definitions already gives the real reason nothing leaks.",
   "issue": "The implementation note claims `frobeniusSchurIndicator_eq_representation` is proved by a parenthesised `(rfl)` \"which keeps the definitional equality inside this module instead of exporting it.\" This is false: in term mode `(rfl)` and `rfl` are identical, and parentheses do not affect whether the defeq is exported (that is governed by `@[expose]`/reducibility, which the note itself already covers). The comment misstates why the proof works and invites a cargo-cult `(rfl)` idiom.",
